-- title:
--   Ramification index n transported across a constant-field square
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$, $k$, $F$, $\mathcal F$, $F'$ be fields with $k$ a separable algebraic extension of $\kappa$, and with $\kappa$-algebra $F$ and $k$-algebras $\mathcal F$, $F'$. Let $G$ be a finite group acting faithfully on $F$ by ring automorphisms, fixing the image of $\kappa$ in $F$ pointwise, and write $F^G$ for the fixed subfield. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $F$ which is a discrete valuation ring and contains the image of $\kappa$, let $n\in\mathbb N$, and assume the contraction $P\cap F^G$ (the preimage of $P$ under the inclusion $F^G\hookrightarrow F$) is also a discrete valuation ring. The two arithmetic hypotheses on the $G$-orbit of $P$ are: (i) for every $g\in G$, every valuation subring $Q=g\cdot P$ and every ring homomorphism $j:P\cap F^G\to Q$ compatible with the inclusions into $F$, the ideal of $Q$ generated by the image under $j$ of the maximal ideal of $P\cap F^G$ equals $\mathfrak m_Q^{\,n}$; (ii) every valuation subring $Q\neq\top$ of $F$ with the same intersection with $F^G$ as $P$ (membership of elements of $F^G$ in $Q$ and in $P$ being equivalent) is of the form $g\cdot P$. Let $\theta_E:F^G\to\mathcal F$, $\varphi:F\to F'$ and $\iota:\mathcal F\to F'$ be ring homomorphisms with $\iota\circ\theta_E=\varphi|_{F^G}$, each compatible with the constant fields ($\theta_E$ and $\varphi$ send the image of $c\in\kappa$ to the image of $c$ in $\mathcal F$, resp. $F'$, via $k$, and $\iota$ is $k$-linear on constants), such that $\mathcal F$ is generated as a $k$-algebra by the range of $\theta_E$ and $F'$ by the range of $\varphi$, and such that $F'$ is finite and separable over $\mathcal F$ for the algebra structure given by $\iota$. Finally let $w$ be a place of $\mathcal F$ over $k$, i.e. a valuation subring of $\mathcal F$ that is a principal ideal ring, is not all of $\mathcal F$ and contains the image of $k$, and assume that for $e\in F^G$ one has $\theta_E(e)\in w$ if and only if $e\in P$. Then there is a place $x'$ of $F'$ over $k$ such that, for all $f\in\mathcal F$, $\iota f$ lies in the valuation subring of $x'$ exactly when $f$ lies in that of $w$, and $\operatorname{ord}_{x'}(\iota f)=n\cdot\operatorname{ord}_w(f)$, where $\operatorname{ord}$ denotes minus the logarithm of the adic valuation attached to the place.
--
--   This is the transport of a ramification index across a constant-field extension: the local invariant $n$ attached to the $G$-orbit of $P$ in $F/F^G$ is shown to persist, with the same multiplier, for a place of $F'$ lying over the given place $w$ of $\mathcal F$. It is used in the computation of the cardinality of inertia groups on integral models of the modular curves $X_0$.
